  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to challenge, to confront, to take on",
      "explanation": "To boldly face a difficult opponent, task, or situation. Implies courage and determination in the face of difficulty. Often used with に to mark the challenge being faced."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "12708_idomu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{課題|かだい}に{挑|いど}む。",
      "english": "I take on a new challenge.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12708_idomu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{世界|せかい}チャンピオンに{挑|いど}む{若|わか}い{選手|せんしゅ}がいる。",
      "english": "There is a young athlete challenging the world champion.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12708_idomu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{失敗|しっぱい}を{恐|おそ}れず、{何度|なんど}でも{挑|いど}む{姿勢|しせい}が{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "It is important to have the attitude of taking on challenges again and again without fearing failure.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The challenge or opponent is marked with に: Xに{挑|いど}む.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{挑|いど}んでいる describes an ongoing challenge or confrontation.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xに{挑|いど}む: to challenge X, to take on X\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {試合|しあい}に{挑|いど}む: to take on a match\n- {記録|きろく}に{挑|いど}む: to attempt to break a record\n- {難題|なんだい}に{挑|いど}む: to tackle a difficult problem\n- {挑|いど}む{姿勢|しせい}: a challenging attitude, willingness to take on challenges\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {挑戦|ちょうせん}する: to challenge (suru verb, more common in everyday speech)\n- {立|た}ち{向|む}かう: to stand up against, to confront",
